WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.934
-Lacey!
-Hi!

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome to the show.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.067
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.501
-I'm so psyched
to have you here.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:08.701
We just had -- Lindsay Lohan
was just on the show.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.267
-Yes.
-And we were talking about

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.067
"Mean Girls."
And we showed --

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:16.767
Yeah, we showed a picture of --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.801
The "Jingle Bell Rock" scene.
-My goodness.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.267
-Would you ever do
a "Mean Girls" reboot?

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.234
-Oh, absolutely.
I think it --

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You would?

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.968
You'd have to, right?
-I mean, I think it would be

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.767
so much fun to see
where these women are now

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.767
and if their kids
are the new mean girls.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.901
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.133
I would love to know
what they're doing.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.501
-Tina, if you're watching,
yeah, let's do it, yeah.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.834
Do people always
come up to you and go,

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.033
"You can't make fetch happen."
-Yes.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.067
Every day of my life.
-Every day of your life, really?

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.267
Everyone knows --
They go --

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.434
-Yes, everyone's like,
"Oh, that's so fetch."

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:51.367
I was even sick recently
and picking up a prescription,

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.133
and the pharmacist goes,
"Oh, you look like you don't

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:56.667
feel very fetch today."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.033
-I have to say --
they say you're

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.901
Queen of the Christmas
Hallmark movies.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.734
And you really are fantastic
in these movies, by the way.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.367
How many have you done?

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.567
-I've done 33 for Hallmark now.
-I've seen all of them.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.334
-Have you really?
-I've seen all of them.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.000
And you are fantastic.
-You're so kind.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.534
You know what?
Do you want to be in one?

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.801
I have some stuff next year.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.300
Like, I would love to be
in one with you.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.400
-Yes! I would love to be in a
Hallmark -- are you kidding me?

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.601
Let's make this happen.
-Let's do it.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.968
Why not?
-Everything is --

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.467
Why do you think
people love it so much?

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.434
Is it just 'cause it makes
you happy, or what is it?

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.133
-I think, now more than ever,

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:34.334
like, we just need
some goodness in the world.

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:35.634
And it's like people sit down

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.167
in their living rooms
for two hours.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.634
They give you their time.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.367
And they're
left feeling uplifted.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.167
-Yeah.
-And, you know, it's joyful.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.767
That's why I love
being a part of them.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.501
And people come up to me all the
time, and they go, "You know,

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:46.901
it's my husband and I,

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.234
it's our favorite thing
to do together.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.100
This movie has helped
bring my family together,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.334
the tradition of watching them."

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.701
So I consider it an honor
to be a part of.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.033
-I watch them with my dad.
-You do?

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.534
-Yeah, he likes them, too.
-I love that.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:00.133
-I watch them with my wife, too.
And I watch them by myself.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.968
I just love -- I'm obsessed.
I'm obsessed.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:05.000
-Thank you so much.
-But how do you do 33?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.234
What's the schedule like?
-Oh, my word.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.000
Okay. So the schedule
is fast and furious.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.200
We do them in 15 days,
and it's --

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.767
-Wow.
-Yeah. It's really long days.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.167
And sometimes they air, like,
two months after we filmed it.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.701
-But are you
all over around the world?

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.133
Are you in Italy?
Are you in --

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.734
-Yes. Oftentimes, we are.
-Wow.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.367
-I've been to Belgium.
I did one in South Africa.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.701
That was amazing.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.434
We were staying on the reserve
where we were filming.

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.267
And, I mean, you'd have
to peek out the door

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.467
to make sure the giraffe wasn't
right in front of your door.

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:30.534
It was magical.
-Really?

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.834
-Everything that
my character discovered

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:34.334
in that movie was really me.
I didn't have to act.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.100
-"The Wedding Veil" trilogy.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.200
This is three of the
most-watched Hallmark movies

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.067
of all time, starring you.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.934
I'm a fan of that.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.767
I think I got word
to your people.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.801
Just say, "Hey, by the way,
I'm loving it right now.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.100
Don't spoil it.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.300
I want to watch
the whole trilogy."

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.634
-Thank you so much.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.234
-But you have an announcement
to make for any fans.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.400
-Yes, Autumn Reeser
and Ali Sweeney and I,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.467
we are gonna be back with
three more "Wedding Veils."

00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:00.767
We're currently filming them.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.801
-Come on!
-Yeah.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.467
We're currently filming
the last one.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.367
We're about to actually
head to Greece this weekend

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:09.367
to film the third one.
But Ali is the lead-in.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.667
And we are so excited to bring
these characters back to life.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.133
Because the movies
always end with a kiss,

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.334
they fall in love.

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.200
And now we get to see
what happened after that.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.267
There might be babies,
the friendships are deeper.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.801
And so, January 7th,
the first one is premiering.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.167
-Congrats on that.
[ Applause ]

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.601
Can we talk about
your new Christmas project?

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.767
-Absolutely.
-This is "Haul Out the Holly."

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.534
Can you tell everyone
what this one's about?

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:33.367
-Well, my character goes home
hoping to just relax

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.267
and be home for Christmas
and watch Christmas movies

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:38.501
and do nothing Christmas-related
in the neighborhood.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.868
'Cause where she's from,
the HOA department

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:43.434
of the cul-de-sac is, like,
crazy about Christmas.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:44.701
-Yeah.
-They go all-out.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:47.033
She gets, you know,
pulled into the activities.

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.634
And this is the first time
I've done a Christmas movie

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:49.968
that's a comedy.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.234
-It's a wonderful cast.
Melissa Peterman, Wes Brown,

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.167
Stephen Tobolowsky,
Ellen Travolta.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.234
These amazing people that just
made me laugh all day.

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:58.767
-And you get to do some physical
comedy, which I do love.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.300
I'm a fan.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.400
Here's Lacey Chabert
in "Haul Out the Holly."

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.801
Take a look at this.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.868
-I was wondering
when you'd like to meet

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.300
to plan the snowman parade.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.567
-Right.
Uh, how about later tonight?

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.167
-No.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.367
No.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.234
I never plan anything
after the cookie contest.

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:17.801
-Oh, okay.
Why not?

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:20.501
-If I lose, I'll be
in no condition to do anything.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:21.934
-Good for you for being honest.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.734
-But I've never lost.
-Right, no, of course.

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.834
Okay.
So, uh, if you win --

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:28.033
-"If"?
If I win?

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.534
-Sorry, sorry, sorry.
No, I mean, when --

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.501
-Okay, don't jinx me.
-Right.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:34.400
-Just --
-Please. Mmm.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.434
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.767
Lacey Chabert,
"Haul Out the Holly"

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.868
premieres this Saturday
at 8:00 p.m.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.167
on Hallmark Channel.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.133
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.300
Stick around, everybody!

